<title>NORWAY: Kvaerner group in Turkey bridge talks.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner group in Turkey bridge talks.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Norwegian construction and engineering company Kvaerner ASA said on Thursday a Kvaerner-led consortium had been chosen to negotiate for a seven billion crown road and bridge contract in Turkey.  </p>
<p>Kvaerner said the consortium, comprising British, Japanese and Turkish companies, were in talks with the Turkish roads department for the project in the Izmit bay.</p>
<p>The company added that it expected its share of the deal to be around one third of the total value.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
